# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the InfraCtrl Next.js application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Package added to `package.json` dependencies
- `package-lock.json` updated with new dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Integration
**Modified: `app/layout.js`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag, following Vercel's official documentation

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified this project uses Next.js App Router with JavaScript
- Added Analytics component to the root layout file (`app/layout.js`)
- Positioned the component after existing elements but before closing `</body>` tag

## Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Production build completed successfully with no errors
✅ **Linter**: No linting errors introduced in `app/layout.js`
✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file properly updated with `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1`
✅ **Code Quality**: Changes preserve existing code structure and patterns

## Notes

- The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals
- Analytics data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard once deployed
- No environment variables or additional configuration required
- The component is lightweight and optimized for performance

## Files Modified

1. `frontend/app/layout.js` - Added Analytics import and component
2. `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
3. `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated dependency lock file
